WEBVTT

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:40.650
<b><u>Episode 11</u></b>

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.650
The Resolve of Yama Juugo

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.240
Bastard...

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.870
What is that look in your eyes?

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.080
Now I'll shatter your right elbow.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.010
Come on, act like it really hurts.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.260
It's no fun if you don't.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:03.930
You look pathetic.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.810
You were hiding a gun on you, too?

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.590
You're some girlfriend.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.670
Don't worry. They're rubber bullets.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.280
They hurt like hell, though.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.240
And you think that'll scare me?

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.030
I have a proposal.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.330
What would that be, girlfriend?

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.340
Why don't we end this fight here?

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.740
Sounds like a sweet deal for you.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.890
Now that I've come this far, 
I'm seeing this through.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.000
You sure about that?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.970
I've figured out what
 your power really is.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.970
What'd you say?

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.180
Your power comes from
 Nanana's Collection, doesn't it?

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.930
If that's what you think,
 then tell me what it "really is."

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.890
Unfortunately, I can't tell you that yet.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.810
Bluffing again?

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:56.030
No. Keeping quiet is my bargaining chip.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.480
What do you mean?

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.080
Damn it!

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.040
<i>He can still move after 
getting injured that much?</i>

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.970
May I continue?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.140
If I reveal the secret

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.920
to your power now,
 you won't be able to use it.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.360
And then Juugo would
 bare his fangs at you again.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.350
But I can't deny the
 possibility that you still have

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.850
another ace up your sleeve.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.130
Then it would just be a grueling match.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.040
The fight wouldn't end 
until one of you goes down.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.060
Therefore, I propose we end it now.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.900
Cut the crap, Tensai!

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:41.730
Tell me! I'm going to... 
kill him... right here...

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.230
Sorry, but I absolutely hate gambling.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.570
Unless you can convince me,
 I don't intend to listen to you.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.620
You can't... trust me?!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:54.680
Nope.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:58.710
I haven't sunk so low that I would 
trust a guy who can barely speak.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.670
Now, back to the subject.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.390
In sum, this is what I'm saying:

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:14.520
Please let us go.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.660
That's awfully high and mighty of you.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.820
That's just how I am. Think nothing of it.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.610
And if I refuse?

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:24.830
Then the gambling begins.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.330
But I have no intention of betting 
my life in a place like this.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.930
I want to fight on a much grander stage.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.130
I do agree with that.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.790
Dying here would not be worth it.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.280
Then we agree. So what is your answer?

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.180
Fine. It's over.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.070
And one more thing.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.300
Swear that you will not
 go near Yoshino Saki again.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.940
Understood.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:54.420
I don't want to be mistaken 
for a stalker anymore, anyway.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.520
Good.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.510
By the way, I never caught your name.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.730
Would you tell me, girlfriend?

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.950
Ikkyuu Tensai, master detective!

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.340
I see.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.700
I'll remember that, 
brilliant master detective.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.540
And your name is?

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.960
What? You didn't know?

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.130
I know, but you never 
introduced yourself to me.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.840
I see.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.340
Then I will introduce myself.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.390
I'm Ikusaba Hiiyo.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.190
And your real name?

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:29.800
Huh? It's Ikusaba Hiiyo...

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.540
I see. I'll remember that.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.020
Looks like your life's
 been saved, Yama-kun.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.900
You should be grateful
 to your lovely girlfriend.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.610
I won't forget this, Ikusaba Hiiyo...

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.880
I could say the same to you, Yama Juugo.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:46.820
I acknowledge that

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.420
you are my enemy.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.130
<i>I can't believe that she
 could really figure out its power.</i>

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.820
<i>The Whisper of the Death God...</i>

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.720
<i>The ace up my sleeve that lets me induce</i>

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.040
<i>powerful suggestions upon my enemy.</i>

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:12.620
Ikusaba-san...

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.040
What is it, Four-Eyes?

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.060
There's something I need to say to you.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.890
When I was in the original Adventure Club,

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.320
there was nothing that I wanted for myself.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.450
Just because I was an Adventure Club member,

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.200
I believed that I was one of the heroes.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:35.990
But when Konjou-senpai gave me 
this Nanana's Collection treasure,

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.410
I was shocked.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:42.070
She must have already
 known that I was just a

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.290
phony with no real goals.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.350
Isn't that still true now?

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:47.620
No.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.510
Then what is it you want?

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:53.760
To surpass all of you

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.720
and become number one.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.650
My wish is to surpass all
 the challengers on this island,

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:05.320
like you and Konjou-senpai, 
who seek Nanana's Collection.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:11.280
And that is why you seek Nanana's Collection?

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:16.230
I want a world in which
 no one stands in front of me!

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:20.400
To surpass us and become number one, eh?

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:25.020
Of course, more new members have joined

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.420
who I'm sure I'll have to defeat.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.430
I have no right to stop
 someone who wants to do something,

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.920
nor do I intend to.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.350
Best of luck.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:38.050
See you later, Yuiga.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.790
<i>One day, I'll surpass you.</i>

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.190
What's that defiant look in your eyes?

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:54.330
I don't wanna hear it. Shut up.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.160
It was a draw this time. Just accept it.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.320
What was his Nanana's 
Collection treasure, anyway?

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:05.970
No idea.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.200
Then, when you said...

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.780
Yeah, I bluffed.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.540
Saying I couldn't trust you 
was a form of bluffing, too,

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.050
so don't worry.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.360
It's not like it bothered me at all.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.520
Is that so? Okay, then.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.940
Still, I can't believe you 
bet on a bluff like that.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.980
You must hate gambling.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.980
No, that's not it. I had a reason.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.590
Think about it.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.090
Why did Ikusaba refrain from

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.700
using such an awesome 
power until the very end?

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:39.770
He could have used it to beat his 
opponents to a pulp, just like this.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.440
It was his trump card, right?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.740
Exactly.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:45.250
That's why he didn't use it at the start.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.400
But it's clearly strange that 
he didn't use it at all until he

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.710
was backed into a corner.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:57.920
Thus, we can infer that his 
power must have some weakness.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:58.890
Meaning...

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.350
Meaning?

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:04.030
That was his last trump card.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:06.310
So he had no choice
 but to accept my proposal.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.230
There you have it.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.820
By the way, Juugo...

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.350
I bet you could look over toward where

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.400
Ibara-dono is lying there, 
sleeptalking, and see her panties.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.550
Huh?! Where?! Which way?!

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.610
Ah... Isshin-sama...
 This is too sudden...

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:23.210
I was obviously lying, you pervert.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:24.550
Stop! Seriously, stop!

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:25.740
Does it hurt that much?

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.100
Yes, damn it!

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.610
Really? Then I'll touch it some more.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.210
Hurry up and pass
 out from lack of oxygen.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.130
I'll clear the ruins for you.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.090
Well, in any case...

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.800
I'm glad you're alive, Juugo.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:44.020
If you died here,
 I'd lose my rival, you know.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.580
Right...

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:57.630
That treasure chest was just awful, though.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.660
It was?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.270
The puzzle was just for decoration.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:04.090
Just a dummy that came
 off easily with nothing to solve.

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:06.080
It wasn't even locked.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.870
That is pretty awful.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:10.530
I've had enough of ruins for a while.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:12.590
For things that are so hard
 to spot, they're really tiring.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.420
Definitely not worth the trouble.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.480
That sounds just like you, Tensai-chan.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:23.890
So, was there anything 
unusual about this one?

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.760
Juugo doesn't tell me very much lately.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.650
I'm sure he's hiding
 something from me...

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.210
If I had to say...

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:39.080
It was the first time we fought with 
someone not in the Adventure Club.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.490
Oh? Who was it?

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.790
His name was Ikusaba Hiiyo.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.320
I see...

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.080
So that's why.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.220
What is it?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.020
Nothing.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.000
So, anyway, Tensai-chan...

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.540
Want to make a bet?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:00.190
Congratulations on
 getting out of the hospital.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.000
Do you really mean—

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.640
I'm just being polite, of course.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.700
When did my injuries heal, anyway?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.570
You were never injured in the first place,

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.740
so there was nothing to heal.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.820
This is the Nanana's
 Collection treasure from the ruins.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:21.030
It's apparently called, "You Can
 See Things That Happened in the Past."

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.820
Same type of name as always...

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.370
Wait, huh?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.800
Are you serious?!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.170
That's definitely what Nanana-dono said.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:34.700
She also said that either
 you or I could keep this one.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.610
What about President Yuiga?

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.440
He passed on it.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:42.760
Seems he's happy enough just 
having driven Ikusaba Hiiyo away.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.350
I see...

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:48.770
So, Juugo, do you want that treasure?

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:53.800
No matter what its power is,

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.480
you must never use it.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.870
You promised Nanana-dono, eh?

00:11:58.870 --> 00:11:59.510
Yeah.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.490
But you look like you want it.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:03.350
I really want it, actually.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:07.570
Then why not break your promise?

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:12.520
Nanana-dono can't take a
 step out of that room, anyway.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:14.040
She'll never find out.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.050
Well, whatever. You decide what to do.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.730
I don't care either way.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.260
You sure?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:25.510
Wouldn't it be useful to 
you as a master detective?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.290
With that power, I could 
solve any case instantly!

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.480
But that's no fun.

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.430
So I don't need that.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:37.770
Tensai.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:38.650
What?

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.440
You don't want it?

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:44.350
I promised Nanana-chan.

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:47.280
So I can't take that.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:50.710
Why not just keep it in secret?

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:54.460
Sneaking around committing
 evil deeds is your specialty, right?

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.790
I don't do that!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.560
Don't say that! Here!

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.920
I told you, I don't want it.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:01.280
Here, here! Here, here!

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.850
You're hiding something, aren't you?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.090
Tsk. I guess I lost.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.260
What?

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.560
I bet Nanana-dono a month's worth of

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.330
pudding against a
 month's worth of coffee milk.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:14.370
On what?

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.970
Whether you'd keep
 your promise to her or not.

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:19.410
Are you serious?!

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:21.030
That was close...

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.330
By the way, I lied about its power.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:24.740
You did?

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:27.820
It's actually called the Evil Spirit Ward.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.950
Its official name is
 Shard of the Sacred Lance.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:34.140
It contains a shard of a
 sacred lance and wards off evil.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.000
What "evil"?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.170
You know, Nanana-dono said

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.920
that you would definitely keep your promise.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.350
I see.

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:47.140
I was sure you'd break it, though.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.140
I see.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.590
Tensai!

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:51.560
Here.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.060
By the way, if Nanana-chan had lost,

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.850
how was she planning to
 get you all that coffee milk?

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.300
By having you pay for it, obviously.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.570
Of course.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.550
Also...

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:10.470
Make up some excuse to tell her
 why I didn't get her pudding for her.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.080
I'm not going home today.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.410
You're a real jerk.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:17.140
A master detective never loses!

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.330
Get it right!

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:25.530
<i>If that treasure really had been</i>

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.880
<i>"You Can See Things That 
Happened in the Past,"</i>

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:32.010
<i>and if I hadn't made that 
promise with Nanana-chan,</i>

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.350
<i>what would I have done?</i>

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.810
<i>If it would help me
 find Nanana-chan's killer,</i>

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.310
<i>of course I should use it...</i>

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:39.970
<i>No, that's not right.</i>

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:43.590
<i>Wanting to help Nanana-chan 
without knowing what she really</i>

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.280
<i>wants is just me indulging my own ego.</i>

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:49.990
<i>Then I'd be no different from Ikusaba,
 who was just using her.</i>

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.620
<i>I need to ask her and find out.</i>

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:02.130
I'm home.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.090
Welcome back.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.480
Here you go.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:07.300
Ah, thanks!

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:10.010
Hey, how'd the bet go?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.230
You won.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.560
So you kept your promise.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:16.470
I keep my promises.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.690
That's why I need to talk to you.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.170
'Bout what?

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:25.420
I promised that I would find your killer.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.360
I did it because I want to help you.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.460
So I want to know for sure.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.920
Do you want to pass on?

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.590
What do you want to happen?

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.330
Where's this coming from?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.290
Answer me. What do you want to do?

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.740
What do I want to do?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.620
I'll leave that to you.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.470
That's not good enough!

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:49.510
Tell me how you really feel!

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.720
What's gotten into you?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.430
It's because you're so 
pushy that girls don't—

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.430
Fine.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.460
I want a battle, Nanana-chan!

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.390
A battle?

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.780
Basically no-holds-barred.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:04.350
You win if you get your 
opponent to admit defeat.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.360
Why?

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.290
If I win, you'll tell 
me what you really want.

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:11.490
And if you win...
 everything stays as is!

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:12.990
And no going invisible!

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:14.800
Fight me seriously!

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:16.950
Sounds like fun.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.650
Okay. I'll take you on.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:22.450
Do you think you can beat me?

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.000
I will win!

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:26.960
Here we go.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:28.150
Yeah!

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.840
Come on!
 You think you can beat me that way?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.260
Damn it! Quit darting around!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.900
You can't catch me!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:41.740
Why are you so serious about this?

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:43.270
I told you!

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:46.110
I want to know what you really want!

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.150
Oh, hell!

00:16:58.790 --> 00:16:59.830
Ow, ow!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.540
Looks like it's over.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:02.200
I'll break it this time.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:06.040
Go ahead! Break it if 
you can, you NEET ghost!

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.920
Why'd you say it that way?!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.640
You're making me mad!

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:12.340
Why are you being so stubborn?

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:15.980
Because I want you to tell 
me what you really want!

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.430
What do you want to do?!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.810
I told you, I'll leave that to you!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:23.640
If I don't hear it from you, 
I'll never have the resolve!

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:26.710
If you pass on,
 you'll disappear from this room, right?

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:28.150
If that happened, I'd miss you!

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.100
That would be painful!

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:33.020
But if you really want to move on

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:36.170
and I hesitate for my own
 reasons and put off helping you,

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.280
that's just me feeding my ego!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.950
That's why I want to know what you want!

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:42.690
If you're gonna break my arm, do it!

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:44.770
But I'll challenge you again tomorrow!

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.310
And if I lose again, then the next day!

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:49.130
I'll challenge you every day until I win!

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.010
Nanana-chan?

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:01.680
I give up.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.310
What I really want is...

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:13.260
I want to find my killer, 
and kill them myself.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.690
That's how I really feel.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.210
But I don't know if I'd
 immediately move on after that or not.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.870
There's something else now
 that I don't want to leave behind.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.140
Something else?

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.820
How this island will change,

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:33.050
what will happen to the 
people who come here...

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:36.510
I want to watch it a little longer now.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.010
That includes you, Juugo.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:49.800
I mean, this island turned out to 
be a lot more fun than I imagined!

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.610
I guess that's how I really feel.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.140
Nanana-chan...

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:02.280
Back to drinking.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.540
If that last treasure really had been

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.210
"You Can See Things That 
Happened in the Past,"

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:12.980
would you still have told me not to use it?

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:14.710
What do you mean?

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:18.990
If I used that, I could 
find your killer, right?

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.640
I might be able to help you move on.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:25.270
Would you still tell me not to use it?

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:26.870
I would.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:27.890
Why?

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:31.180
Because it was a
 promise between you and me.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.560
Even if we never found 
your killer because of it?

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:36.270
I believe

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:40.280
that you'd find the killer, 
even without using that.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.330
By the way, does that artifact really exist?

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:47.410
Who knows?

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.110
What?

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:50.830
It does!

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.160
Why do you say that?

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:55.010
You said "even without 
using that," didn't you?

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.290
Did I?

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:57.370
You did!

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:00.970
If it didn't exist, you'd say
 "a thing like that," or something!

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:03.180
All right! I'm gonna go find it!

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:07.300
You're not going to ask where it is?

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:10.160
You wouldn't tell me anyway, would you?

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.600
I guess not.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.990
That's fine!

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:16.110
I'll find it in my own way!

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:17.200
I'm off!

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.350
See you later.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:28.810
Huh? Shiki-san?

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:30.670
Why are you sleeping out here?

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:34.270
Hey, Juugo, take me to my room.

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:37.190
Man, you're a pain! No way!

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:39.000
You're mean.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:39.880
Hey! Tensai!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.000
Idiot! Keep your voice down!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.600
Nanana-chan was really mad, you know.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:49.680
Maybe I shouldn't have come 
back yet, after all...

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:51.810
Let's just go buy her pudding.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:55.690
Damn it, Daruku! Are you 
telling me to admit defeat?!

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.330
Admit it!

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:03.170
Don't forget my pudding!

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.450
<b>Yoshino Saki</b>

00:22:37.230 --> 00:22:40.500
I don't want to die.
 I don't want to die.
